+<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy & Data Controls">
+    <h2>1. Privacy by Design &amp; Data Minimization</h2>
+    <p>
+        We treat privacy as a foundational architectural requirement rather than a legal checkbox. Our systems are privacy-protective by default:
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Data Minimization:</strong> We collect only the bare minimum data required for an immediate user-initiated task. Anonymous visitors can browse articles without having session cookies set automatically.</li>
+        <li><strong>Fuzzed &amp; Coarse Granularity:</strong> Where optional demographic or statistical signals are used, we collect coarse brackets (such as age brackets) and apply differential privacy noise to aggregate article view counts.</li>
+        <li><strong>Purpose Limitation &amp; Short Retention:</strong> Session state for the Reading List expires automatically after 24 hours (<code>ttl: 86400</code>) and is deleted immediately when emptied or when you sign out.</li>
+        <li><strong>Zero Device Fingerprinting:</strong> We never use canvas rendering, font enumeration, or full <code>navigator.userAgent</code> string sniffing to track your device. When capability checks are needed, we rely on standard JavaScript feature detection and User-Agent Client Hints (<code>navigator.userAgentData</code>).</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>2. Cookies, Session Security &amp; Partitioned State (CHIPS)</h2>
+    <p>
+        We do not store sensitive tokens or Personally Identifiable Information (PII) in <code>localStorage</code>. First-party sessions use <code>__Host-</code> prefixed, <code>HttpOnly</code>, <code>Secure</code>, <code>SameSite=Lax</code> cookies restricted to <code>Path=/</code>. If any cross-site 1:1 embed preferences are stored, they use <strong>CHIPS (Cookies Having Independent Partitioned State)</strong> with the <code>Partitioned</code> attribute so state is never shared across top-level sites.
+    </p>
+
+    <h2>3. Third-Party Audits &amp; Embed Mitigations</h2>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>No Third-Party Trackers on Sensitive Pages:</strong> Third-party ad and analytics scripts are strictly excluded from authentication (<code>/signin</code>, <code>/signup</code>) and legal/privacy management pages.</li>
+        <li><strong>Video Façade Pattern:</strong> Multimedia embeds display a static local preview first and only connect to <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> when you explicitly click play.</li>
+        <li><strong>SDK-Free Social Sharing &amp; FedCM:</strong> Social share links are plain static anchors without third-party JavaScript SDKs, and federated sign-in uses the browser-mediated <strong>Federated Credential Management API (FedCM)</strong>.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2 id="permissions">4. Declarative Browser Permissions (PEPC)</h2>
+    <p>
+        We disable powerful browser features (camera, microphone, geolocation, interest-cohort) by default via the <code>Permissions-Policy</code> HTTP header. If you optionally want to personalize local news weather/edition alerts, permission is only requested through a user-initiated control such as the declarative <strong>Page Embedded Permission Control (<code>&lt;permission&gt;</code>)</strong> element:
+    </p>
